  migrations/000184_charging_si.up.sql:81). The `drives` table has
  PRIMARY KEY (id) with id BIGSERIAL — the snapshotWriter's
  ON CONFLICT (vehicle_id, ts) would never fire and every Write
  would INSERT a fresh row, multiplying drive count by tick count.
  Pointing the writer at `drives` is therefore not just naming-wrong
  but architecturally incompatible.

